.TH WTDB 1 "2026-06-14" "wtdb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wtdb \- give every git worktree its own database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wtdb
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wtdb
isolates the local development database per git worktree. When a worktree is
created it copies the dev database into a new one named after the worktree,
rewrites the database connection variable in the worktree's env file, and copies
configured gitignored paths (such as
.IR node_modules ).
.PP
This keeps migration state separated across concurrent worktrees, so a migration
run on one branch never mutates the schema another branch relies on. It hooks
into plain
.B git worktree add
via a
.I post-checkout
hook, so no new git commands are needed.
.PP
Database copying is provided by adapters. A PostgreSQL adapter ships in the box,
copying via a near\-instant
.B CREATE DATABASE ... TEMPLATE
and falling back to
.BR pg_dump (1)
/
.BR psql (1)
when needed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Scaffold a starter
.I .wtdb.json
in the current repository.
.TP
.B install
Install the
.I post-checkout
git hook so new worktrees are provisioned automatically. Idempotent.
.TP
.B sync
Provision the current worktree now: copy the database, write the env file, and
clone configured paths.
.TP
.B prune
Drop databases whose worktrees have been removed.
.TP
.B status
List the worktrees wtdb has provisioned and their databases.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
A repository is enabled by adding a
.I .wtdb.json
file at its root with three keys:
.TP
.B envFile
The dotenv\-format file to copy and rewrite (for example
.I .env
or
.IR .dev.vars ).
.TP
.B dbEnvVar
The variable in that file holding the
.I postgres://
connection URL.
.TP
.B pathsToCopy
A list of gitignored directories or files to bring into each new worktree.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "envFile": ".dev.vars",
  "dbEnvVar": "DATABASE_URL",
  "pathsToCopy": ["node_modules"]
}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Enable wtdb in a repository:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wtdb init
wtdb install
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a worktree (provisioned automatically by the hook):
.PP
.RS
.nf
git worktree add ../myapp-feature
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove a worktree and reclaim its database:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git worktree remove ../myapp-feature
wtdb prune
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .wtdb.json
Per\-repository configuration, at the repository root.
.TP
.I .git/wtdb/state.json
Internal registry mapping worktree paths to provisioned databases.
.TP
.I .git/hooks/post-checkout
Git hook installed by
.BR "wtdb install" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-worktree (1),
.BR psql (1),
.BR pg_dump (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Will Hackett. Source and issues: https://github.com/willhackett/wtdb
